{"declarations":[{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Constructions/CasesOn.html#Lean.mkCasesOn\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">mkCasesOn</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">declName</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.Name\">Name</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Basic.html#Lean.Meta.MetaM\">MetaM</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Unit\">Unit</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Constructions/CasesOn.html#Lean.mkCasesOn","kind":"def","line":71,"name":"Lean.mkCasesOn","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/11acb17ec6b07a8f9e9173e6845197929540936b/src/Lean/Meta/Constructions/CasesOn.lean#L71-L81"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Constructions/CasesOn.html#Lean.mkCasesOnViaProjs?\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">mkCasesOnViaProjs?</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">declName</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.Name\">Name</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Basic.html#Lean.Meta.MetaM\">MetaM</a> <span class=\"fn\">(<a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Option\">Option</a> <a href=\"./Lean/Declaration.html#Lean.DefinitionVal\">DefinitionVal</a>)</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Builds a `casesOn`-shaped eliminator for `declName` out of structure projections, or returns `none`\nif `isCasesOnViaProjs` does not hold.\n\n`I.casesOn … t minor` as built from `I.rec` reduces only once `t` reduces to a constructor\napplication, which for a proposition it may never do: proofs are opaque. Applying the minor premise\nto the projections of `t` instead sidesteps that. The minor premise expects the fields of\n`I.mk x₁ … xₙ` rather than those of `t`, but both are proofs of the same proposition, so proof\nirrelevance identifies them.\n\nThe result has the same shape as `mkCasesOnImp` produces: parameters, motive, major premise, minor\npremise. It also matches `recOn`, since the type is not recursive.\n","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Constructions/CasesOn.html#Lean.mkCasesOnViaProjs?","kind":"def","line":35,"name":"Lean.mkCasesOnViaProjs?","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/11acb17ec6b07a8f9e9173e6845197929540936b/src/Lean/Meta/Constructions/CasesOn.lean#L35-L69"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Constructions/CasesOn.html#Lean.isCasesOnViaProjs\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">isCasesOnViaProjs</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">declName</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.Name\">Name</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Basic.html#Lean.Meta.MetaM\">MetaM</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Whether `casesOn` for `declName` is built by `mkCasesOnViaProjs?` rather than from the recursor.\n\nA single constructor and no indices make the type structure-like, and large elimination then forces\nevery field to be a proof, which is what makes the projections available: projecting data out of a\nproposition is what `Exists` may not do.\n","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Constructions/CasesOn.html#Lean.isCasesOnViaProjs","kind":"def","line":21,"name":"Lean.isCasesOnViaProjs","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/11acb17ec6b07a8f9e9173e6845197929540936b/src/Lean/Meta/Constructions/CasesOn.lean#L21-L33"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">opaque</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Constructions/CasesOn.html#Lean.mkCasesOnImp\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">mkCasesOnImp</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">env</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Environment.html#Lean.Kernel.Environment\">Kernel.Environment</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">declName</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.Name\">Name</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Except\">Except</a> <a href=\"./Lean/Environment.html#Lean.Kernel.Exception\">Kernel.Exception</a> <a href=\"./Lean/Declaration.html#Lean.Declaration\">Declaration</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Constructions/CasesOn.html#Lean.mkCasesOnImp","kind":"opaque","line":17,"name":"Lean.mkCasesOnImp","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/11acb17ec6b07a8f9e9173e6845197929540936b/src/Lean/Meta/Constructions/CasesOn.lean#L17-L17"}}],"imports":["Lean.AddDecl","Lean.Meta.Basic","Lean.Meta.InferType"],"instances":[],"name":"Lean.Meta.Constructions.CasesOn"}